  "passage": "Ms. Carter gave her students a strange homework assignment. \"Choose one thing you dislike doing,\" she said. \"Do it for one minute every day.\"\nStudents chose different things: cleaning desks, reading English, stretching, practicing piano, or washing dishes.\nAt first, one minute seemed too short to matter. But after a week, many students found that starting was the hardest part. Once they began, they often continued longer.\nJerry, who hated reading, started with one minute a day. By the third week, he read ten minutes without noticing.\nMs. Carter explained that the rule was not magic. It only made big tasks feel less scary.\nA minute cannot finish everything, but it can open the door.",
